---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<Layout title="Website information and terms" simpleFooter>
  <article class="legal-page"><p class="eyebrow">Before you travel</p><h1>A little <em>clarity.</em></h1><p>These notes explain the scope of this website. They are not booking terms or a travel contract.</p><h2>Inspiration, not an offer</h2><p>Destination photography and suggested experiences are illustrative. They do not confirm a particular property, supplier relationship, itinerary, inclusion, price or available departure. Every proposed arrangement requires separate discussion and confirmation.</p><h2>Your journey brief</h2><p>The planner produces a file for you to keep. {site.enquiryEndpoint ? 'Downloading it, and sending your brief to Pardus, does not reserve a service, take payment or create a contract with Pardus.' : 'Downloading it does not send an enquiry, reserve a service, take payment or create a contract with Pardus.'}</p><h2>Travel requirements</h2><p>Entry, visa, health and documentation requirements depend on your circumstances and can change. Verify applicable requirements with official authorities before arranging travel. Guidance cannot guarantee a visa decision or permission to enter a destination.</p><h2>Bookings and cancellations</h2><p>Before any booking or payment, request the confirmed itinerary, price, applicable supplier terms, payment schedule and cancellation conditions. Those details are not established by this website.</p><h2>Website content</h2><p>Images and brand assets are used to present the Pardus travel concept. The business should confirm its final content, asset permissions and complete customer-facing legal terms as operational services are connected.</p></article>
</Layout>
